# Pairs with NewbornPinEventuallyUsable. The claim-head conjunct of Armed is off
# by one: it asks the activation to have read the record at its claim head, not
# below it. The newborn's replay is driven only to the head below, so arming is
# never enabled, and its own appends are never covered. It edits the Armed
# predicate, not an action, so it names no perturbed action.
MODULE: NewbornPinEventuallyUsableArmingNeverEnabled
TARGET: NewbornPinEventuallyUsable
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: arming asks for a read at the claim head, which no driven replay reaches
BOUNDS: WithPreArm = FALSE

--- FIND
    /\ IF WithPreArm THEN rp[a] >= seenP[a] ELSE rp[a] >= claimHead[a] - 1
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: off by one: the record at the claim head must have been read.
    /\ IF WithPreArm THEN rp[a] >= seenP[a] ELSE rp[a] >= claimHead[a]
--- END
